      "message": "The idea about `user_id` in the url was to allow a cloud admin to GET user\u0027s application credentials.\n\nThe interesting thing about this change is that it promotes application credentials from a day-2 authentication mechanism to a primary authentication mechanism: before you had to sign in with other methods to issue and use the application credentials. The idea might be interesting, but i do not understand the implications of it. What if the user is locked out? Are the application credentials limited or unlimited in this case? I feel that this change needs a spec.\n\nAnd the change definitely needs tests.",
